%S A400869 1,3,3,10,3,9,10,36,3,9,9,30,10,30,36,136,3,9,9,30,9,27,30,108,10,30,
%T A400869 30,100,36,108,136,528,3,9,9,30,9,27,30,108,9,27,27,90,30,90,108,408,
%U A400869 10,30,30,100,30,90,100,360,36,108,108,360,136,408,528,2080,3,9
%N A400869 The number of ordered pairs (k_1, k_2) of nonnegative integers bitwise covered by n such that k_1 + k_2 is also bitwise covered by n.
%C A400869 A number k is bitwise covered by n if and only if bitand(n, k) = k, i.e., all the 1-bits in the binary expansion of k occur in the same position as in the binary expansion of n.
%C A400869 a(n) depends only on the lengths of runs of 1's in its binary expansion. It does not depend on the order of these lengths. Each run of length k in the binary expansion of n contributes a factor 2^(k-1)*(2^k+1) to a(n) (see the second formula).
%H A400869 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A400869/b400869.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%F A400869 a(n) = Sum_{k_1,k_2=0..n} T(n, k_1) * T(n, k_2) * T(n, k_1 + k_2), where T(n, k) = 1 if bitand(n, k) = k, and 0 otherwise (A090971).
%F A400869 a(n) = Product_{k = 1..A069010(n)} A007582(A245562(n,k)).
%F A400869 a(n) = A400870(p^n) for any prime p.
%F A400869 a(2^n) = 3 for n >= 0, and a(n) > 3 for any positive n that is not a power of 2.
%F A400869 a(2^n-1) = A007582(n).
%F A400869 a(2^n+1) = 9 for n >= 2.
%F A400869 a(k*2^n) = a(k).
%F A400869 a(n) = 3^A000120(n) if and only if n is a Fibbinary number (A003714).
%F A400869 a(n) is even if and only if n is not a Fibbinary number (A004780).
%F A400869 A007814(a(n)) = A014081(n).
%t A400869 a[n_] := Product[2^(k-1)*(2^k+1), {k, Length /@ Select[Split[IntegerDigits[n, 2]], First[#] == 1 &]}]; Array[a, 66, 0]
%o A400869 (PARI) lengths(n) = {my(b = binary(n), r = []); for(i = 1, #b, if(b[i], if(i == 1 || !b[i-1], r = concat(r, 1), r[#r]++))); r;}
%o A400869 f(k) = 2^(k-1)*(2^k+1);
%o A400869 a(n) = my(r = lengths(n)); prod(i = 1, #r, f(r[i]));
%Y A400869 Cf. A000120, A001316, A003714, A004780, A007283, A007582, A007814, A014081, A069010, A080099, A090971, A245562, A400870.
